Spoilers follow:

>
>1. what's a good way to get turn to stone resistance.. I've eaten
>   dozens of lizards with no success. (is my luck just bad?)

Lizards do not give you intrinsic resistance to stone-turning.  Nothing does
that.  Keep them in your pack.  They will save your buns only if you eat
them instantly after you begin getting "stiff".

>2. what is the exact object of the game... I remember playing an old version
>   where you had to escape the dungeon with the amulet of Yendor.

That is still the object, only now there is a suprise waiting on "level 0"
(which you will never see if you go up from level 1 without the amulet.

In addition, there are a couple of intermediate quests for you:  loot the
tower of Vlad the Impaler, and loot the treasure rooms of the castle.

>3. Where can I expect special levels? I've gotten to 26 and died several times
>   even after killing medusa... i've heard about the tower and the castle?

In Hell.  The exact location changes.

>4. How about where I find the wizard of yendor? am I even close yet (level 26)

You need telepathy, a blindfold, and a mirror.  Once you kill Medusa, the
mirror will tell you generally where the wizard is, if you properly apply
it.

>5. what are you supposed to do with a unicorn horn?

Same thing you do with any tool, apply it to stuff.

Cures what ails you, if you apply it to yourself.  Eliminates harmful potions
when #dipped in them.  Rustproof weapon.  Also can sometimes do a 1-point
"restore ability" if you loose strength or such.

Good luck,
